>> .ije le cmana ze'e stali ba le mo'u pu'u
>> rolcfari fu'o (And these mountains have been here from the beginning.)
>
>And the mountain for the whole of time to come <le mo'u pu'u>
>
>I don't get mo'u pu'u.  Explain?

I would translate {rolcfari} as something like: "x1 is everything starting
to occur",
so {pu'u rolcfari} would be "the process of everything starting", and
{mo'u pu'u rolcfari} marks the completion point of that process.
So {ba le mo'u pu'u rolcfari} means "after the completion of the process
of everything starting", or "from the beginning" for short.

